====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|physical}} Matter, material.
## A [[quantity]] of [[matter]] [[cohere|cohering]] together so as to make one [[body]], or an [[aggregation]] of [[particle]]s or things which collectively make one body or quantity, usually of considerable size.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1718|origyear=1704|author={{w|Sir Isaac Newton|Isaac Newton}}|title=w:Opticks|edition=2nd|passage=And if it were not for theſe Principles the Bodies of the Earth, Planets, Comets, Sun, and all things in them would grow cold and freeze, and become inactive '''Maſſes''' ; {{...}}.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1821|author=w:George Buchanan|by=an unnamed translator|termlang=la|original=Rerum Scoticarum Historia|origyear=1582|title=The History of Scotland, from the Earliest Accounts of that Nation, to the Reign of King James VI|volume=1|page=133|passage={{...}} and because a deep '''mass''' of continual sea is slower stirred to rage.}}
## {{lb|en|obsolete}} Precious [[metal]], especially [[gold]] or [[silver]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1596|author=w:Edmund Spenser|title=w:The Faerie Queene|section=IV.10|passage=Right in the midst the Goddesse selfe did stand / Upon an altar of some costly '''masse''' […].}}
## {{lb|en|physics}} A measure of the [[inertia]] of a mass of [[matter]], one of four fundamental [[property|properties]] of [[matter]]. [[SI]] unit of mass: [[kilogram]].
## {{lb|en|pharmaceutical drug}} A [[medicinal]] [[substance]] made into a [[cohesive]], [[homogeneous]] lump, of [[consistency]] suitable for making pills; as, blue mass.
## {{lb|en|medicine}} A [[palpable]] or visible abnormal [[globular]] structure; a [[tumor]].
## {{lb|en|bodybuilding}} Excess body weight, especially in the form of [[muscle]] [[hypertrophy]].
##* {{quote-journal|en|year=1988|author=Steve Holman|title=Christian Conquers Columbus|journal=[[w:Iron Man (magazine)|Ironman]]|volume=47|issue=6|pages=28–34|passage=After all, muscle maniacs go "ga ga" over '''mass''' no matter how it's presented.}}
## {{lb|en|proscribed}} {{synonym of|en|weight}}
# A large [[quantity]]; a [[sum]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1829|author=Sir {{w|Walter Raleigh}}|title=The Works of Sir Walter Ralegh, Kt|volume=VIII|passage={{...}}he hath discovered to me the way to five or six of the richest mines which the Spaniard hath, and whence all the '''mass''' of gold that comes into Spain in effect is drawn.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1869|author=w:Alexander George Richey|title=Lectures on the History of Ireland: Down to A. D. 1534|page=204|passage=For though he had spent a huge '''mass''' of treasure in transporting his army, {{...}}.}}
## [[bulk|Bulk]]; [[magnitude]]; body; [[size]].
##* {{quote-book|en|year=c.1599-1601|author=w:William Shakespeare|title=[[s:The Tragedy of Hamlet, Prince of Denmark/Act 4|The Tragedy of Hamlet, Prince of Denmark]]|section=act 4, scene 4|passage=Witness this army of such '''mass''' and charge / Led by a delicate and tender prince,}}
## The [[principal]] part; the main body.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1881|author=w:Thucydides|translator=w:Benjamin Jowett|title=Thucydides translated into English|volume=1|page=310|passage=Night closed upon the pursuit, and aided the '''mass''' of the fugitives in their escape.}}
## A large body of individuals, especially persons.
##* {{quote-song|en|year=1970|artist=w:Black Sabbath|title=w:War Pigs|album=Paranoid|text=Generals gathered in their '''masses''' / Just like witches at black masses}}
##: {{ux|en|The '''mass''' of spectators didn't see the infraction on the field.}}
##: {{ux|en|A '''mass''' of ships converged on the beaches of Dunkirk.}}
## {{lb|en|in the plural}} The lower classes of persons.
##: {{ux|en|The '''masses''' are revolting.}}

