#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=John Horne|title=A Companion to World War I|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=5sm0LLZMzegC&pg=PA159&dq=%22increasingly+mass%22&hl=en&ei=GjqDTdT3Gs_JcYDo9ZsD&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=81&ved=0CNYDEOgBMFA#v=onepage&q=%22increasingly%20mass%22&f=false|page=159|passage=The air arms did more than provide the warring nations with individual heroes, for their individual exploits occurred within the context of an increasingly '''mass''' aerial effort in a war of the masses.}}
# Involving a mass of people; of, for, or by the masses.
#: {{ux|en|'''Mass''' unemployment resulted from the financial collapse.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1958|title=Child Welfare|volume=37|page=2|passage=Every agency is sold on use of '''mass''' media today — or at least, it thinks it is — and what can be "'''masser'''" than television?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1970|author=James Wilson White|title=The Sōkagakkai and Mass Society|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=FEdxm4SgQbAC&pg=PA3&dq=%22fully+mass%22&hl=en&ei=nQuCTbC7GsePcfaxpIwD&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ved=0CDgQ6AEwAw#v=onepage&q=%22fully%20mass%22&f=false|page=3|passage=While agreeing with Bell on the unlikelihood that any fully '''mass''' — in the sense of atomized and alienated — society has ever existed,<sup>5</sup> I believe that at any point in time, in any social system, some elements may be characterized as "masses."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1974|author=Edward Abraham Cohn|title=The Political Economy of Environmental Enhancement|page=91|passage=Undoubtedly this is the case; at least it is "'''masser'''" than in Pinchot's time.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1999|month=December|author=Sara Miles|title=Rebel with a Cause|journal=[[w:Out (magazine)|Out]]|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=WWIEAAAAMBAJ&pg=PA132&dq=%22formerly+mass%22&hl=en&ei=NZ-CTeDtKMj4cZHh_Y8D&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=30&ved=0CK0BEOgBMB0#v=onepage&q=%22formerly%20mass%22&f=false|page=132|passage=But it also highlights the changes that have taken place in gay and AIDS activism, and the way that a formerly '''mass''' movement has been recast.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Howie Klein|title=Queer as role models|journal=The Advocate|issue=825|date=21 November 2000|page=9|passage=The director didn't make the images up; they're there, but in putting that one slice of gay life into the '''massest''' of '''mass''' media — the amoral promiscuity, the drug and alcohol abuse, the stereotyped flamboyance and campiness, the bitchy queeniness and flimsy values — something very dangerous happens {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Brian Moeran|title=Asian Media Productions|page=13|passage={{...}} if only because it promises the ‘'''massest'''’ of '''mass''' markets.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=John R. Hall|title=Gone from the Promised Land: Jonestown in American Cultural History|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=ZgWh_E1f0asC&pg=PA79&dq=%22overwhelmingly+mass%22&hl=en&ei=0QWCTc7CJ4j6cJ-hoYMD&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CD4Q6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=%22overwhelmingly%20mass%22&f=false|page=79|passage=Finally, in the past century, secular culture itself has undergone a transition from predominantly folk styles to an overwhelmingly '''mass''' culture, {{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Thomas Peele|title=Queer popular culture: literature, media, film, and television|page=11|passage=As a right, we come to expect it, and that happens through the '''mass''' media, the '''massest''' of which, by far, is television.}}

